[M5.6] Python-vs-Extension comparison (same algorithm, same dedup)
------------------------------------------------------------------------
Both crawlers reach the SAME backend write path, so M4's idempotency evidence
covers the extension's submit path:
  - Python:  scrape_khamenei.py submit_to_backend -> /api/khamenei/submit
  - Extension: content_khamenei.js extractAndSubmit -> /api/phase2/complete (site=khamenei)
  Both land in _phase2_save_khamenei (server.py:458), which dedups on
  speech_id + content_hash(content|date) and requires a non-empty date to
  'skip' (server.py:485) — the exact predicate M4 proved idempotent (re-run ->
  0 inserted / N skipped, 0 errors).
Identical algorithm constants on both sides:
  - year list URL:  https://farsi.khamenei.ir/speech?nt=2&year=YYYY  (one year = one page)
  - item selection: only anchors whose first element is a skyText date span
    (datedSpeechLinks / LIST_ITEM_RE) — sidebar widgets without a date excluded
  - digit normalization: Persian/Arabic-Indic -> ASCII (toAsciiDigits / to_ascii_digits)
  - date validation: Jalali YYYY/MM/DD; year derived from the date prefix
  - auto walk: descending years, STOP after 2 consecutive empty years (proven by
    node tests M5.3: "two consecutive empty years: stop (reason=empty)")
  - MIN_YEAR floor handled (node tests: "below MIN_YEAR -> floor")
Live proof that an extension-shaped payload dedups against the M4 Python data:
  phase2/complete x2 -> skipped/skipped, counts unchanged (M5.5).
Conclusion: the extension would produce the SAME 1400=35 / 1402=56 and create
NO duplicates on re-run, because it shares the proven backend dedup.

